$ Scalar masses at their own DOF. Three independent systems, hand eigenvalues k / m:
$ - scalar points 1 and 2 (IDs below the grids'): CELAS4 k = 12 and 10 to the held scalar point 9, CMASS4 1.5 and 2.5:
$   lambda = 8 and 4;
$ - two CMASS4 of 1.5 and 2.5 on scalar point 31, CELAS4 k = 12 to the held scalar point 39: lambda = 12 / 4 = 3;
$ - a CMASS2 of 2 on grid 5's T3 (its only free DOF), CELAS2 k = 10 in T3 to the held grid 99: lambda = 5.
$ Expected eigenvalues 3, 4, 5, 8. Masses at another DOF, or only the first of two masses at one DOF, change them.
SOL 103
CEND
TITLE = SCALAR MASSES AT THEIR OWN DOF
METHOD = 1
SPC = 1
BEGIN BULK
EIGR,1,GIV,,,,4
GRID,5,,0.,0.,0.,,12456
GRID,99,,1.,0.,0.,,123456
SPOINT,1,2,9,31,39
SPC1,1,0,9,39
CELAS4,11,12.,1,9
CELAS4,12,10.,2,9
CMASS4,21,1.5,1
CMASS4,22,2.5,2
CELAS4,13,12.,31,39
CMASS4,23,1.5,31
CMASS4,24,2.5,31
CELAS2,14,10.,5,3,99,3
CMASS2,25,2.,5,3
ENDDATA
